From 63cdc05dc33590af6618be7fee4dc1a72f51aa99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:17:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Nibe: predictive pre-heat, degree-minutes floor, price-peak
 reduction, anti-flap, legionella guard
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Combines three phases of work on core/nibe/decision.py's two comfort
levers (space-heating curve offset + DHW "Lyxläge varmvatten"), all
still gated behind nibe.enabled (default off) so nothing here changes
behavior for anyone until explicitly turned on in Settings.

Fas 4c (2026-09-25) — predictive pre-heat (THIRD LEVER)
    decide_heating_boost() gains an independent exception,
    "engaged_price_spike_ahead": pre-heats the curve when a genuine
    upcoming price spike (top price_spike_percentile of known prices,
    and at least price_spike_min_delta_ore above the current price) is
    forecast within price_spike_lookahead_hours. Gated by its own
    nibe.price_spike_boost_enabled flag. Checked after the existing
    solar-surplus/cheap-price checks so it never overrides either.
    Inspired in part by github.com/Samot89/
    Smart-NIBE-Control-a-Home-Assistant-MQTT's own pre-heat idea.

Fas 4d (2026-09-26) — degree-minutes floor (FOURTH LEVER)
    number.degree_minutes_16_bit_43005 enabled and confirmed live.
    decide_heating_boost() gains a ceiling check (not a new exception):
    a degree_minutes reading at/below degree_minutes_floor (default
    -400.0, a conservative first guess) blocks any of the three boost
    branches, since a boost is exactly the wrong move while the
    compressor is already under enough load to risk triggering electric
    addition. Not gated by its own enabled flag — it can only make the
    system MORE conservative, so it's live whenever nibe.enabled is on.

Fas 4e (2026-09-26) — three items from that day's GitHub/HA-Community
competitive scan (claude/omvarldsbevakning-nibe-github-2026-09-26.md),
picked by Håkan as items 1-3 of that report's recommendation list:

  1. Active price-peak reduction (FIFTH LEVER). decide_heating_boost()
     gains "reduced_expensive_price": during a genuinely expensive hour
     (top expensive_price_percentile of today's prices, default 0.85),
     actively pulls the curve offset negative by heat_offset_reduction_c
     (default -2, its own independent constant) instead of only ever
     holding at neutral. Gated by its own nibe.price_reduction_enabled
     flag, off by default. Checked after the three boost branches (never
     overrides a proven boost) and deliberately NOT gated by the
     degree-minutes floor — a negative offset only reduces compressor
     demand, which that floor has no reason to block.

  2. Upgrade hysteresis / anti-flap (SIXTH section), mirroring
     tengmo-ab/smart-heat-control's own two-years-in-production pattern:
     any *increase* in heat_offset_c within upgrade_cooldown_s (default
     1200s / 20 minutes, matching their reported figure) of the last
     change is suppressed and held at the previous value
     ("suppressed_anti_flap"); a decrease always applies instantly.
     Wraps only the comfort outcome (solar/cheap/spike/reduction/normal)
     — never the hard safety statuses (no_data, watchdog_reset,
     no_headroom, blocked_low_degree_minutes), which always take effect
     immediately regardless of cooldown. New backend/app.py state:
     nibe_heat_offset_last_applied_c / nibe_heat_offset_last_changed_monotonic.

  3. DHW legionella/disinfection guard (SEVENTH section), inspired by
     tvofi/heatpump_optimizer's treatment of legionella disinfection as
     a non-negotiable MPC constraint. decide_dhw_luxury() forces
     comfort_mode="normal" (never "luxury") once continuous Economy time
     exceeds max_continuous_economy_s (default 259200s / 3 days, an
     explicitly unconfirmed defense-in-depth guess, not a measured value
     for this pump/installation). Deliberately overrides governor
     headroom too, unlike every other check in this module — judged an
     acceptable trade given it fires at most once every several days.
     New backend/app.py state: nibe_dhw_last_non_economy_monotonic, with
     first-tick initialization so a fresh start doesn't read as either
     "never economy" or "already over the limit".

Testing: core/nibe/tests/test_decision.py grows from 32 to 61 tests
(all passing) covering the price-spike and degree-minutes-floor
behavior (Fas 4c/4d) plus 18 new cases for the three Fas 4e items,
including their interactions with each other and with the existing
levers (e.g. anti-flap never suppressing a hard safety status, price
reduction not blocked by the DM floor, the legionella guard overriding
no_headroom).

Settings: core/bess/settings_store.py's nibe section gains
price_reduction_enabled / expensive_price_percentile /
heat_offset_reduction_c / upgrade_cooldown_s / max_continuous_economy_s,
all backfilled for existing installs via _migrate_schema() with
no-behavior-change-on-upgrade defaults. backend/api.py validates each
new numeric setting.

